--- body ---
## Context

Child of 0817. The rung-3 driver runs its scenario on four Menagerie documents
(`--fixture-documents`). The rung is the whole corpus — 114 attachments today,
two more when 0794 lands (not blocked on it).

## Actions

1. Import the full Menagerie package; no truncation.
2. After the run settles, read every attachment's status through
   `Zotero.SDTPackSitter.inspect(id)` (`scheduler.js` status classes; exposed
   in `bootstrap.js`) and assert none is left `queued`: each ends `indexed` or
   `unindexed` (a pack) or `failed` / `outOfScope` (a named reason), recorded
   per attachment. No new sitter-side plumbing.
3. Replace the four-document timeouts with named, documented ones sized for
   the whole corpus (the 900 s index default was tuned for four small files);
   a run that times out says so rather than reading as a sitter failure.
4. Run 0816's integrity check over the run.

## Test

Red first: a payload that leaves one attachment `queued` after settling must
fail the completeness assertion.

## Exit criteria

A recorded whole-Menagerie run with every attachment accounted for and the
integrity check green.
